    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": "Header Section"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The Header section is a key part of a website that houses the logo and navigation links, providing a consistent identity and easy navigation for visitors to explore the website."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "For the header section, you'll include:"
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet_list",
      "items": [
        "Logo - We'll simply use the text \"Jane\", but feel free to use your own name or logo.",
        "Navigation Links - Links for the Projects and Contact sections."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The design for the header section is shown below:"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "alt": "Layout of the header section",
      "src": "data:image/png;base64,"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "As discussed previously, you'll use the <header> tag to structure the header section."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Similarly, you can place the logo using <div> and use <nav>—another semantic tag—to organize the navigation links."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Here's how the basic header structure looks:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "html",
      "content": "1<header class=\"header\">\n2    <div class=\"logo\">Jane</div>\n3    <nav class=\"nav\">\n4        <a href=\"#projects\">Projects</a>\n5        <a href=\"#contact\">Contact</a>\n6    </nav>\n7</header>"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "How does it work?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Use this space for your doubts about this lesson. Ask us anything that's confusing and our experts will provide explanations to help you understand."
    }
